  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Given that $f(9.6)=3$ and $f(10.4)=11,$ find an approximation for ${f}^{\u2032}(10).$",
  "worked_solution": "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\n{f}^{\u2032}(x)\u2248\\frac{f(x+h)-f(x-h)}{2h}\n$$\n\n \nat the point $x=10$ with the step size $h=0.4.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(x) & \u2248\\frac{f(x+h)-f(x-h)}{2h} \\\\ {f}^{\u2032}(10) & \u2248\\frac{f(10+0.4)-f(10-0.4)}{2(0.4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(10.4)-f(9.6)}{0.8} \\\\  & =\\frac{11-3}{0.8} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{0.8} \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
